## Finding register - corrected by STEP 2

STEP 1's F-108-3 over-reported: 5 of its 7 hits were test assertions (chat/tests.py) and docstring lines. Corrected, genuine live-COUNT findings:

- **F-108-1 - No block-user feature.** The presentation (slide 10) lists Block & Report for chat; P-107 blocker A2; required by Apple 1.2 and Google UGC policy. Status: OPEN GAP (default), needs a new part (backend + Flutter).
- **F-108-2 - No account deletion.** P-107 blocker A1; required by Apple 5.1.1(v) and Google Play. Status: OPEN GAP (default), needs a new part (backend + Flutter, plus a public deletion URL).
- **F-108-3a - Story view_count is a live COUNT** (stories/views.py:161, owner-only endpoint). It was specified verbatim by P-049 but never recorded as an exception to Section 5.4. Status: OPEN GAP (default) - either denormalize with an atomic F() update on first view, or have Ahmed document it as a deliberate exception.
- **F-108-3b - Chat unread_count is a live COUNT per conversation** (chat/serializers.py:349), evaluated on every conversation-list request. It is per-user derived data rather than a shared counter, but still a live COUNT. Status: OPEN GAP (default), same decision.
- **F-108-4 - Section 7 contradiction.** P-105 says a public staging URL/domain exists and an uptime monitor was verified; P-104/P-106/P-107 say VPS and domain are still open. Needs Ahmed's clarification (see Part C).
- **F-108-5 - Manager naming.** Section 5 says .objects.published(); the code uses PublishedManager exposed as published_objects (content/models.py), used in feed/services.py and search/services.py. Same gating, different name; documented here, not a violation.
